    "narrative": "The LawDog lineup is headlined by **Cal Raleigh** (79.31) and **Bryce Harper** (75.38), both of whom benefit from prime situational alignment. **Cal Raleigh** is our strongest play, leveraging a high-ceiling matchup against Lopez, who carries a shaky 4.77 xERA; combined with the favorable park factor and a cleanup spot, he is primed for damage. Similarly, **Bryce Harper** draws a strong environment against Holmes. While **Lawrence Butler** (66.89) and **Luis Arraez** (65.61) also project well, **Lawrence Butler** specifically warrants attention for his +10% park boost and +13% platoon edge against Miller, making him a high-efficiency anchor for our 5x5 production today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Jung Hoo Lee** (49.39) and **Dylan Beavers** (49.13). While **Jung Hoo Lee** received a significant +10% boost due to wind conditions, the underlying quality of the opposing starter, Pivetta, kept his total efficiency score behind our final utility options. We opted for the higher daily floor of our starters, particularly in categories where we cannot afford dead weight as we push through the final stretch of the season. We remain cautious of the bottom of our order, specifically **Masyn Winn** (47.08) and **Alex Freeland** (42.86), whose scores are dragged down by their placement in the #9 hole. While we are leaning on their efficiency to bridge the gap, they are the first to be evaluated if we need to pinch-hit for a high-leverage stolen base opportunity later in the day.\n\nRegarding risk, there are no immediate weather threats to report, but we are monitoring the matchup against Miller closely; despite a favorable park factor, his ability to suppress production requires us to watch **Zack Gelof** and **Lawrence Butler** early. We are also keeping a close watch on **Justin Crawford**, whose speed is vital for our scarcity needs in SB, even though his spot at the bottom of the order yields a -8% penalty to his overall projection. The lack of availability for **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Matt Chapman** continues to compress our bench flexibility, putting the onus on our healthy starters to maintain our Roto standing.",
